Just as important as WHERE you are going to put your Primary Port is the KIND of Primary Port you will build. For your first Primary Port, it is highly recommended to build an Outpost. Regardless of what kind of construction you choose, you will have 28 days to build the Primary Port. You and/or your group of Commanders will be able to calibrate your ability to/enthusiasm for building based on this metric.

Tier 1 Outpost Primary Port: ~22.5k Tons of Commodities
Pro: (Relatively) fast to build. Can set up initial supplies for further building
Con: Outpost only has Medium landing pads
Con: No Shipyards
Con: [Trailblazers 3.3]: Requires additional infrastructure to unlock certain services, including the commodity Market.

Tier 2 (Coriolis, Asteroid Base) Primary Port
Pro: You get Large Pads and more commodities than the Outpost equivalent
Pro: Has Most system services on board [Trailblazers 3.3. Unlocks most Services system-wide?]
Con: It is 70,000+ tons, and if you and/or your group are not fans of hauling it may be a struggle to finish within time.

Tier 3 (Orbis, Apollo, Artemis) Primary Port: 210k+ Tons of Commodities
Pro: Large Pads for all.
Pro: Build a Tier 3 Primary Port and get the links set up properly and you will probably never run out of any of its commodities unless you get a CG next door.
Pro: Should have all the services on board [Trailblazers 3.3. Unlock all services system-wide?]
Pro: Bragging Rights.
Con: It is 210,000 Tons worth of Commodities that at present can only be hauled ~784 tons at a time. I hope you and/or your group have some time to haul your asses off.

Tier 2 (Asteroid Base Specifically) Primary Port: ~70k Tons of Commodities
Pro (Asteroid Base): Default Extraction Economy
Pro (Asteroid Base): ASTEROID BASE!
Pro (Asteroid Base): Fulfills the 1 Extraction Economy construction required to spawn resource sites.
Con (Asteroid Base): Default Extraction Economy
Con (Asteroid Base): Can only be built in an Asteroid Ring/Planetary Ring
Con (Asteroid Base): Must approach from the correct “side” of the Asteroid Belt/Planetary Ring or travel ~50 km further. Generally Galactic Up. If you are not in the core, align by aiming towards the brighter, less dusty side.
Con (Asteroid Base): Approach in Frame Shift Drive mode may be slowed more dramatically if you get too close to the Planetary Ring
Con (Asteroid Base): Which Rocky/Icy/Metal variant you get is supposed to correlate to the kind of asteroid belt/planetary ring you build the Asteroid Base in. At the time of writing, which Planetary Ring (if more than one is present) you will hit is unreliable at best.
Con (Asteroid Base): Extraction Bonus of the Planetary ring/Asteroid Belt is not added to the economy of the Asteroid Base itself.
